SlopWorld on Debian
==================

The package stages the mod at /usr/share/slopworld/SlopWorld. As your normal
user, attach it to a separately installed native Linux RimWorld 1.6 game:

  RIMWORLD=/path/to/RimWorld/game
  slopworld mod install --game "$RIMWORLD"
  systemctl --user daemon-reload
  systemctl --user enable --now slopd.service
  slopworld

The installer saves the game directory as the launcher default. The source defaults to
`/usr/share/slopworld/SlopWorld`; use `--source DIR` for another mod tree.
You can omit --game when RIMWORLD is exported or the game path is already saved.
Enable SlopWorld in the launched game's mod list. After package upgrades, refresh
the mod, reload the user unit, and restart the daemon as your normal user:

  slopworld mod install

  systemctl --user daemon-reload
  systemctl --user try-restart slopd.service

Before removal, stop and disable the daemon as your normal user:

  systemctl --user disable --now slopd.service
  slopworld mod uninstall

After package removal, run systemctl --user daemon-reload.
The package leaves per-user configuration, sessions, and game saves intact.
A user unit under ~/.config/systemd/user takes precedence over the packaged
unit; remove a previous source installation's unit before enabling this one.
